<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trībŭlōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		tribulus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>full of thorns</i> or
				<i>thistles</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voragines viarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 3, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			 — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>thorny</i>, <i>rough</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 3</span></i>
			. —<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribulosissima dissimulatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 7 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
